diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 8347b4a..b371200 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,5 +1,35 @@
 # deploy-demo
 
-Deploys the service to AWS on every push to `main`.
+Deploys the service to AWS on every push to `main` and on every pushed
+version tag matching `v*`. It can also be started manually
+(`workflow_dispatch`).
 
 This repository is public.
+
+## AWS authentication
+
+The workflow authenticates with OIDC. It assumes
+`arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/deploy-widget` in `eu-north-1`, and no
+long-lived AWS access keys are stored. The `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` and
+`AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` repository secrets are no longer used and can be
+deleted.
+
+The role's trust policy must trust the GitHub OIDC provider
+(`token.actions.githubusercontent.com`, audience `sts.amazonaws.com`) and
+match the `sub` claim exactly, with no wildcard:
+
+- `repo:<owner>/<repo>:ref:refs/heads/main` for pushes to `main`
+- `repo:<owner>/<repo>:ref:refs/tags/v*` for version tags (use `StringLike`
+  for this one only)
+
+Manual runs from other branches get a different `sub` and are denied unless
+you add it.
+
+## Secrets
+
+- `SLACK_WEBHOOK`: used by the Slack notification step.
+
+## Runner
+
+The job runs on a GitHub-hosted runner (`ubuntu-latest`). Self-hosted runners
+must not be used in a public repository.
